For conversion, scripts/mobile_models/make_models.py (yolox_export_module)
runs this network with decode_in_inference switched off and applies the same
box decoding with constant grids and strides precomputed for the fixed
640 x 640 input, because the grids upstream builds at run time from the
feature map shapes do not convert to Core ML. The converted models carry that
decoding; verify checks it against upstream's own.

The weights these files load (yolox_s.pth, release 0.1.1rc0) are not in this
repository. scripts/mobile_models/make_models.py downloads them from the
official release and checks their SHA-256.
